    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite passes with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city owner capacity rule: creating an owner is rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nChanges, following the existing patterns for `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException`:\n\n1. **`CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending field (`city`), mirroring the other 409-mapped exceptions.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `CityAtCapacityException` to a `409 Conflict` `ProblemDetail` with an `errors` array naming the `city` field.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (handles `POST /api/owners`) \u2014 added a `requireCityBelowCapacity(...)` check in `addOwner`, invoked right after required-field validation. It counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (consistent with the existing per-city customer-code sequencing) and throws when the count is `>= 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`).\n\nThe rule fires only after the mandatory-field checks, so a request missing/blank fields still gets the usual 400, and a valid 51st owner in a full city gets 409.",
